{%- comment -%}
  One photo on an industry guide — port of the two <figure> blocks in
  IndustryPage() (pages/IndustryPages.jsx).

  The filename is derived from the page handle, which is identical to the React
  slug for all eight guides, so there is nothing per-industry to maintain here:
  /img/industries/<slug>-hero.webp becomes assets/ind-<slug>-hero.webp.

  asset_url does not fail when a file is missing — it happily returns a URL that
  404s — so the onerror keeps React's behaviour of hiding the whole figure
  rather than leaving a broken-image icon in the middle of the article. That
  matters if a ninth industry page is added before its photos are uploaded.

  Usage: {% render 'hnl-industry-photo', slug: h, variant: 'hero', klass: 'hero', alt: '...' %}
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- assign file = 'ind-' | append: slug | append: '-' | append: variant | append: '.webp' -%}
<figure class="ind-art__{{ klass }}">
  <img src="{{ file | asset_url }}"
       alt="{{ alt | escape }}"
       width="1200" height="1200"
       loading="lazy" decoding="async"
       onerror="var f=this.closest('figure'); if(f){f.style.display='none'}">
</figure>
